## Likely follow-up questions

**Q: Quick rejects?**

total % k ≠ 0, or any number > total / k.

**Q: Why largest first?**

Big numbers have the fewest places to go, so dead ends show up early.

**Q: Complexity?**

O(k^n) worst case; with pruning far less. The bitmask DP is O(n · 2ⁿ).

**Q: Bitmask DP?**

dp[mask] = current group's partial sum for the numbers in mask; reachable if some unused number fits.

**Q: Shared state?**

None outside the call.

**Q: n = 40.**

Exponential either way; meet-in-the-middle helps for k = 2 only. Say so.

**Q: Related?**

Partition Equal Subset Sum (k = 2) is a knapsack DP — mention the special case.

